  "independent_block_height_calculus": "Over EVERY characteristic-zero FIELD,for nonzero polynomial phases P_i on independent variable blocks and arbitrary formal constant-coefficient T_i with zero constant symbols,the nilpotence height on product_i P_i^m is SUM_i h_i(m) for operator SUM_i T_i,MIN_i h_i(m) for operator PRODUCT_i T_i,and floor(h_m/e) for T^e. At the top sum height the ONLY nonzero multinomial allocation is the vector of individual top heights,so its scalar and tensor product are nonzero. All larger powers vanish. Product and power formulas follow directly. Polynomial outputs are retained;no evaluation or cancellation assumption is used. General rings with zero divisors are excluded from this height calculus. Pointwise height sums do NOT by themselves permit adding limsup slopes without synchronized subsequences.",
  "subadditivity_countercontrol": "Nilpotence indices need NOT be subadditive even for PURE SAFE GVC pairs. For EVERY n>=2,r>n,take T=sum_i partial_i^r and P=product_i x_i. Exact monomial allocation gives h_m=n floor(m/r),a_m=h_m+1;degree counting proves cutoff1/(r-n),sharp at m=r*l,Q=x_1^((r-n)m). The least integer cutoff is1. Yet a_r-a_1-a_(r-1)=n-1. Thus n2,r3 already has a3=3>a1+a2=2,and no dimension-free bounded quasi-subadditivity error exists across these pairs. This does NOT rule out an error depending on actual phase/symbol or on dimension/degree. No positive general gap theorem or new safe-family campaign is claimed;this is an exact countercontrol to the proposed shortcut.",
  "false_doubling_gap_construction": "For EVERY M>=1,an explicit eight-variable PURE finite-symbol GVC FAILURE has an arbitrarily long first-shift doubling gap. Let r=2M+3,F=(t+c)(ad+bt),B=partial_t(partial_a partial_d-partial_b partial_c),G=u v w^(r-2),A=partial_u^r+partial_v^r+partial_w^r,P=FG,Lambda=(B+A)^2. Retained DVG1 and the degree1 commutator lemma give h_(B,F)(m)=m-1 for all m. Independent-block height calculus gives h_Lambda(m)=m-1 when s=m modr<=M+1,and m-2 when s>=M+2. Hence ALL pure outputs vanish,Lambda^kP^(k+1)0 for EVERY M+1<=k<=2M,but Lambda^kP^(k+2)!=0 for EVERY k>=1. The fixed marker P^2 is bad at every index. Also with L=M+1,the component-indexed block Lambda^(j-1)P^j0 holds for EVERY L+1<=j<=2L,so an index shift does not rescue the false generic doubling-gap criterion. First-shift nonzero indices recur at k=jr-1. The deficit is bounded1/2 and never tends to infinity,so this is NOT a counterexample to the remaining individual-eventuality=>linearity OP. Phase degree r+3 and operator orders6,r+3,2r do not improve protected endpoints. This disproves transplanting the symmetric-inverse gap rule to arbitrary GVC operators;it does not refute Wrights actual theorem or its Laplacian/HN applications.",
