      "title": "Does formal-symbol eventual safety imply a linear degree cutoff?",
      "scope": "For a formal constant-coefficient symbol over a characteristic-zero field and polynomial phase with all positive pure outputs zero,determine whether eventual vanishing for every individual polynomial multiplier implies some common linear degree bound. Finite polynomial symbols are closed by GVCLINEARCUTOFF20261115;formal quadratic and bounded-degree univariate phases are closed by GVCQUADFORMAL20261115/GVCUNIVFORMAL20261115. GVCHIGHTAIL20261115/GVCJETCERT20261115 characterize the stronger linear-cutoff class by a finite truncation with a tail-order certificate,and GVCFORMALSEMI20261115 gives a theoretical positive semidecision for that class. They do not prove the implication asked here. General formal symbols need not supply the retained algebraic holonomic source. No failure of the implication or positive general theorem is claimed. Nonpolynomial phases/multipliers and variable-coefficient operators are outside this question. GVCBINARYFORMAL20261116 now proves the stronger full pure-to-safe statement for EVERY formal binary symbol and EVERY polynomial phase degree,with optimal fieldC_D. GVCBINARYALLRING20261116 supplies full ordinary finite-jet purity and all-ring uniformity for that entire binary class. Together with prior univariate and all-dimensional quadratic results,the remaining implication is restricted to spatial n>=3 and phase degree>=3. Existing higher-dimensional pure unsafe seeds fail the individual-eventuality premise and are NOT counterexamples to this remaining implication. No positive general theorem or failure of the remaining implication is claimed. GVCALGFORMALLINEAR20261116 closes this implication in EVERY dimension/phase degree whenever the formal symbol is algebraic or a formal UNIT times an algebraic formal symbol. Its exact joint holonomic Taylor source follows from proper factorial diagonals,finite rho evaluation and classical primary-diagonal closure;formal-unit invariance preserves all zero predicates. This is a field conditional-linearity theorem,not full GVC positivity for algebraic symbols or a nonreduced algebraic-family theorem. The remaining n>=3,degree>=3 question therefore requires a principal formal symbol ideal with NO algebraic formal generator up to a unit. Recognizing arbitrary such decompositions and general source producers are not implemented;no general remaining implication or failure is claimed. GVCJOINTSOURCERIGID20261116 now proves the exact ALL-dimensional/ALL-degree source-method boundary:for EVERY NONZERO polynomial phase the FULL raw GVC Taylor source is jointly holonomic iff the formal symbol is algebraic. A gauge and top-output degeneration give a Bessel eigenoperator whose iterates force algebraicity. GVCUNITSOURCEMAX20261116 makes unit stripping plus raw source holonomicity EXACTLY the already closed algebraic-principal-divisor method. GVCQUALNONHOL20261116 gives genuinely nonalgebraic principal divisors with pure phases of every degree and sharp cutoff1,but NONholonomic sources,so individual eventuality cannot force this missing finiteness. These are NOT counterexamples to eventuality-to-linearity. The general implication stays OPEN and requires another mechanism. No new external theorem imported;closure-first and deferred review persist. GVCFORMALCOMM20261116/GVCAPOLARGAP20261116/GVCEXCESSIDEALS20261116 provide a scope-preserving alternative to holonomic sources for the ENTIRE formal-symbol question. Over ALL Q-algebras,finite ad-nilpotence on polynomial coefficients extends the commutator lemma and reduces all markers to EVERY fixed excess-power shift. Over fields,for actual A_m=K[[Z]]/Ann(P^m),h_m=max{k:T^kP^m!=0},b_m=m-h_m:individual eventuality iff b_m->infinity;one linear cutoff iff inf b_m/m>0 iff positive liminf. Thus the full remaining implication is EXACTLY the actual apolar-gap alternative,still OPEN. Ordinary I_(N+1) subset E_N and E_(CD) subset I_C give cofinal cutoff ideals with nilpotents retained,no infinite-ring ACC. Newly audited Flavi